# /model while a turn is still streaming: kiln defers it (it is not on
# internal/tui/app.go's immediateCommandNames, since switching models
# mid-request would change what the running turn is talking to), shows it
# as a queued `you` block, and runs it as a command once the turn ends.
# The in-flight reply finishes on the model that was current when it
# started; the switch takes effect for the NEXT turn. The faux reply is
# held mid-stream, so /model always lands while the turn is busy.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/dialogs-model-switch-mid-stream.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE start the slow turn
KEY enter
WAITFOR /working on it/ 20
SHOT turn-streaming
TYPE /model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /queued\s+\/model/ 20
SHOT model-deferred-while-busy
EXPECT /esc to stop/
EXPECT_NOT /Select model/
RELEASE slow-turn
WAITFOR /Finished the slow turn\./ 20
WAITFOR /Select model/ 20
SHOT dialog-after-turn
EXPECT /Finished the slow turn\./
KEY down
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Now on faux\/faux-2 · small tier/ 20
SHOT switched-for-next-turn
TYPE second turn on the new model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Second turn on faux-2\./ 20
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
